https://github.com/jakobfriedl/BenevolentLoader
(C language, AES-256 payload encryption, Hell's Gate direct syscalls, XOR-protected key with runtime brute-force recovery, API hashing, IAT camouflage, staging from a remote URL.)

# OBJECTIVE
Customize and rebuild BenevolentLoader so that it:
1. Loads an AES-encrypted shellcode blob from a local file named `config.dat` located in the same directory as the loader.
2. Decrypts it at runtime using a FIXED key embedded in the binary — using a key-hiding scheme (the repo's existing XOR-mask + HINT_BYTE brute-force approach must be kept or improved, e.g. key split across sections, derived via a KDF from a constant, or masked with multiple layers; the plaintext key must never appear as a contiguous byte sequence in the binary).
